## Why This Is Asked
Tests end-to-end reliability of streaming reconciliation systems, focusing on critical aspects like idempotency, exactly-once semantics, drift detection, and rollback mechanisms under high throughput conditions—essential for fintech and large-scale payment systems.

## Key Concepts
- End-to-end testing in streaming pipelines
- Idempotent reconciliation and exactly-once semantics
- Drift detection and rollback/replay strategies
- Test data generation for duplicates and out-of-order events
- Performance validation at scale (1M events/sec)

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example: synthetic event generator with duplicates
function genEvents(n){
  const events=[];
  for(let i=0;i<n;i++){
    events.push({id: i, timestamp: Date.now(), amount: Math.random()*1000});
    if(Math.random()<0.1) events.push(events[events.length-1]); // 10% duplicates
  }
  return events.sort(() => Math.random()-0.5); // Shuffle for out-of-order
}
```

